  "body": "**Reported:** press Update on Windows, stop the server with Ctrl+C, nothing happens — the version never changes. PATCH `4.21.4` → `4.21.5`.\n\n## Root cause: process id reuse\n\nThe helper waited with `Get-Process -Id $parent`. Windows recycles pids quickly, and that is exactly what happened — measured live:\n\n```\nPID 38012 IS VISIBLE -> python started 08/01/2026 01:47:00\n```\n\nThe server was stopped at 01:46; an unrelated `python` inherited pid 38012 a minute later. The helper kept waiting on a stranger and never installed. Nondeterministic by nature — which is why this flow sometimes worked and sometimes silently did nothing.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe parent is now pinned by **id + creation time**, read via `GetProcessTimes` and compared against `Process.StartTime.ToFileTimeUtc()`. Same id, different start time ⇒ our parent is gone.\n\nTwo details that matter:\n\n- When the creation time can't be read, the check falls back to the id alone and treats *unknown* as **still alive**. Assuming \"gone\" would install underneath a running server — the exact corruption this whole path exists to prevent.\n- `GetProcessTimes` needs explicit `argtypes` or the handle is truncated on 64-bit and silently returns 0. That bit me during development; it's now asserted by a test comparing the value against PowerShell's.\n\n## Also: retry the install\n\nHandle release isn't instantaneous — an antivirus scan or a slow shutdown can hold the environment briefly. Losing that race left uv having already deleted part of the environment, which is a broken install.\n\nThe install now retries with backoff (0/5/10/20/30s). A later attempt succeeds because the earlier one removed whatever it could, so a transient lock degrades into a *slower* update rather than a broken one. Attempt count is recorded in the result.\n\n## Verification\n\n**Pid reuse, reproduced deliberately** — an unrelated process occupying the pid:\n\n```\nOLD  helper proceeded while pid was occupied: False   ← hangs\nNEW  helper proceeded while pid was occupied: True    ← correct\n```\n\n**Full unattended run** in an isolated `UV_TOOL_DIR`:\n\n```\nenv before : 4.21.5\nstaged     : True\nserver stopped\nresult after ~20s\nhelper     : ok=True exit=0 attempts=1 | Deferred install completed.\nenv after  : 4.21.4\n```\n\nNew tests cover the start-time pinning, the fallback direction, the retry loop, and the `GetProcessTimes`/PowerShell agreement (skipped off Windows). Script rendering is Linux-safe so CI still exercises it.\n\n## Residual risks\n\nThe retry ladder tops out at ~65s of waiting. Something holding the environment longer than that (a stuck process, aggressive endpoint protection) still fails — but it now fails *reporting* a failure with the attempt count, rather than appearing to do nothing.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
