     "date": "2026-07-31T23:05:55Z"
    },
    "message": "fix(updates): identify the parent by start time, and retry the deferred install\n\nReported symptom: press Update on Windows, stop the server with Ctrl+C, and\nnothing happens -- the version never changes.\n\nRoot cause is process id reuse. The helper waited with Get-Process -Id $parent,\nand Windows recycles ids quickly. Measured directly: the server was stopped and\nseconds later an unrelated python process was holding the very same id, so the\nhelper kept waiting on a stranger and never installed. It is nondeterministic by\nnature, which is why the same flow sometimes worked.\n\nThe helper now pins the parent's identity with its creation time as well as its\nid, read via GetProcessTimes and compared against Process.StartTime.\nToFileTimeUtc(). Same id with a different start time means our parent is gone.\nWhen the creation time cannot be read the check falls back to the id alone and\ntreats \"unknown\" as still alive, because assuming the parent has gone would\ninstall underneath a running server -- the exact corruption this path exists to\nprevent. GetProcessTimes needs explicit argtypes or the handle is truncated on\n64-bit and silently returns 0; on non-Windows it short-circuits so the script\nstill renders under Linux CI.\n\nThe install is also retried with backoff (0/5/10/20/30s). Handle release is not\ninstantaneous -- an antivirus scan or slow shutdown can still hold the\nenvironment for a moment -- and losing that race left uv having already deleted\npart of the environment. A later attempt succeeds because the earlier one\nremoved whatever it could, so a transient lock degrades into a slower update\ninstead of a broken install. The attempt count is recorded in the result.\n\nVerified: with an unrelated process occupying the pid, the old logic never\nproceeds and the new logic proceeds correctly. Full unattended run in an\nisolated UV_TOOL_DIR -- stage, stop the server, helper installs by itself:\nok=true, exit_code=0, attempts=1, environment moved 4.21.5 -> 4.21.4 with the\nentry point working.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
